  cache_usage_limits {
    data_storage {
      maximum = 10
      unit    = "GB"
    }

    ecpu_per_second {
      maximum = 5000
    }
  }
}

output "valkey_endpoint" {
  value = aws_elasticache_serverless_cache.web.endpoint
}
```

Connect from the app over **TLS**, and set an expiration on every session and cache key. Treat the store as disposable: your app should handle a missing session or cache entry gracefully.

I’d pick **Amazon ElastiCache Serverless for Valkey**. It’s managed, Redis-compatible, and a good starting point when session and cache traffic may vary. Put it in private subnets and allow connections only from your app’s security group.

