**Pick: Amazon ElastiCache for Redis** — a cluster-mode-disabled replication group (1 primary + 1 replica, Multi-AZ failover). Redis is the right call for sessions because of per-key TTLs (session expiry falls out for free), it's supported natively by every web framework's session store, and it gives you failover. Memcached on ElastiCache has no replication/failover and no TLS/AUTH, which is disqualifying for anything session-related.

One node pair handles an enormous amount of session/cache traffic — you almost certainly don't need cluster-mode (sharding) at launch, and it complicates clients.

