## Worth considering: ElastiCache Serverless

If you'd rather skip node sizing, shard counts, and parameter groups entirely:

```hcl
resource "aws_elasticache_serverless_cache" "sessions" {
  name              = "${var.name_prefix}-${var.environment}-sessions"
  engine            = "redis"
  cache_usage_limits {
    data_storage { maximum = 10 }      # GB
    ecpus_per_second { maximum = 5000 }
  }
  security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.redis.id]
  subnet_group_name  = aws_elasticache_subnet_group.redis.name
}
```

Auto-scales capacity, per-second billing, simpler ops. The tradeoff is less control over eviction policy and shard layout. Happy to go either way — this is the main fork in the road.

